---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<Section
  id="agents"
  title="Your agent reads the logs of the server you started in another tab."
  more={{ href: '/agents/', label: 'More about agents' }}
>
  <p>
    The daemon owns every process, so the stack running in your terminal is reachable from the
    agent's shell: it tails a service's logs, restarts it and runs the tests against the lane, and
    the output stays where you can see it too. An agent working on its own branch starts a lane of
    its own, and its shell can end without the stack dying.
  </p>
  <p>
    A skill teaches the agent the commands, and <code>devlanes mcp</code> gives hosts such as Claude
    Desktop and Cursor the same commands as tools, with a card for the lane.
  </p>
  <Terminal slot="visual" title="agent session">
    <div class="chat">
      <p class="chat-you">checkout 500s on lane 1, see what the api says</p>
      <div class="chat-agent">
        <pre><span class="command">devlanes logs myapp@1:api --tail 100</span>
<span class="failure">TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'callbackUrl')</span>
    at buildRedirect (src/auth/redirect.ts:31:22)
    at registerAuth (src/routes/auth.ts:12:3)</pre>
        <p>
          <code>AUTH_REDIRECT_URL</code> is unset in lane 1, so the fallback at{' '}
          <code>src/auth/redirect.ts:31</code> has no <code>callbackUrl</code>. Fixed the fallback,
          restarting api.
        </p>
        <pre><span class="command">devlanes restart myapp@1:api</span>
<span class="success">ready</span> api  <span class="url">https://api.myapp1.localhost</span></pre>
        <p>
          Checkout answers again on <span class="url">https://myapp1.localhost</span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Terminal>
</Section>
